export default "# ASTRA privacy notice\n\nVersion privacy-1 · 21 October 2026 · applies to the ASTRA Android app (beta)\n\nASTRA is a Vedic astrology and tarot companion run by an independent developer in India. This notice explains, in plain language, what personal data ASTRA uses, why, and how you stay in control. ASTRA is in a closed beta and is free; there are no ads, no payments and nothing is sold.\n\n## What ASTRA uses, and why\n\n- **Birth details** (date, time or time window, birthplace) and **the city you live in**: to calculate your chart, dashas, the Graha Tracker and the panchang. These calculations run on your phone.\n- **Your calculated chart facts** (positions, periods, tone, today's panchang): copied to your private space on the server so Ask ASTRA, Today's line, tarot and Cross-Reading answers can be grounded in your real chart.\n- **My Story** (only if you turn it on): your life stage, what's on your mind, open questions, life events and one-line notes of saved readings. Used to make answers, alerts and check-ins fit your situation. Only the items that fit a question are sent with it, and every answer shows which ones were used.\n- **Your questions and card draws**: sent to the AI to write an answer. They are not kept on the server after the answer is written, unless you save the reading.\n- **Saved readings**: kept on your phone, and backed up to your private space only if you choose \"Back up with Google\".\n- **Account**: an anonymous sign-in, or your Google account if you choose to back up. ASTRA never sees a password.\n- **Usage events**: which screens and features are used (for example \"opened the tracker\", \"answer completed\", \"turned on My Story\"), with your anonymous account ID and app version. They never contain your questions, answers, story, birth details or chart. Used to see whether ASTRA is working and worth continuing. You can switch them off in Me → Privacy.\n- **Error reports**: the type of error and the screen it happened on, without any of your content.\n- **Feedback you send**: the words you write in Me → Send feedback.\n- **Daily counters**: how many questions you've asked today, so the daily limits work.\n\nASTRA does not use your data for advertising, does not sell it, and does not use it to train AI models.\n\n## Who processes it for ASTRA\n\n- **Google Firebase**: sign-in, and your private database space (stored in Mumbai, India).\n- **Google Gemini API**: writes AI answers from your question, chart facts and the story items you allowed. Google processes this to provide the service.\n- **Cloudflare**: runs the AI server, the daily counters, usage events and feedback.\n\nSome of this processing may happen outside India.\n\n## Your choices and rights\n\n- **Turn My Story off** at any time in Me → My Story. It stops being used immediately. Delete it there too.\n- **Switch off usage events** in Me → Privacy.\n- **See and correct** your birth details and story in the app at any time.\n- **Export** your story and chart summary in Me → My Story → Share my story.\n- **Delete your account** in Me → Privacy → Delete my account. This removes your story, chart facts, backups, counters, usage events and feedback from the server, signs you out and clears the app on this phone. Content-free security and usage logs may be kept for up to one year where the law requires it, then erased.\n- **Withdraw consent**: turning a feature off is as easy as turning it on.\n\n## Questions and complaints\n\nWrite to {{CONTACT}}. We will reply within 30 days. If you're not satisfied, you can complain to the Data Protection Board of India.\n\n## Children\n\nASTRA is for adults aged 18 and over.\n\n## Safety\n\nASTRA describes what astrological and tarot traditions say. It does not predict events and is not medical, legal, financial or mental-health advice. If you're struggling, please call Tele-MANAS on 14416 (free, 24x7) or 112 in an emergency.\n\n## Changes\n\nIf this notice changes in a way that matters, the app will show you the new version before it applies.\n";
